IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `P5-section-5`
IMPORT `P5-art-40-41-42`

-- Tests of Articles 40, 41 and 42 (layer 1). Expected values are hand-written from the text, never from the code.
-- Dates: Chapter III Section 5 applies from 2 August 2026 (Art 113 second paragraph, keel fork F-113-groups, assumed).
-- 1 August 2026 is before, 2 August 2026 is the day, 1 September 2027 is after. An AI system placed on 3 December 2027
-- (after 2 December 2027, the date of Chapter III for an Annex III system) is not saved by Art 111(2); one placed on 1 January 2027
-- and not significantly changed is saved on 2 December 2030 (and covered if it was significantly changed).

`Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` MEANS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`

§ `Art 40 to 49 the group applies`

-- The helper only fixes the group; the dates are the keel's.
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` (Date 1 8 2026))
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` (Date 2 8 2026)
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply on the date asked` (Date 1 9 2027)
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2030) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 1 1 2027) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 40 to 49 the provisions apply to the high-risk AI system on the date asked` (Date 2 12 2030) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 1 1 2027) TRUE

§ `Article 40(1): the presumption of conformity with harmonised standards`

-- args: date asked, route, date placed, significantly changed, the AI system's products are covered by Section B of Annex I, the Section B requirements have been integrated, standard is a harmonised standard (Art 3(27)), in conformity, references published, covers the requirement
-- Before the group applies: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- On the day and after: all four conditions met, the presumption arises.
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each condition missing in turn: NOTHING (the text says no presumption arises "to the extent" only; it does not say the system is not in conformity).
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 1 9 2027) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 3 12 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 111(2): placed before the date of application of Chapter III and not significantly changed: saved, NOTHING; changed: covered.
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 2 12 2030) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 1 1 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 40(1) the high-risk AI system is presumed to be in conformity with the requirement set out in Section 2` (Date 2 12 2030) `Art 40 to 49 tests Annex III route` (Date 1 1 2027) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- The general-purpose AI model limb: args: date asked, harmonised standard, in conformity, references published, covers the obligation
